(x+1)=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=-1$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186421141 :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S⇒N:$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x=-1}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is sufficient for}\\,\\underbrace{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x=-1}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is necessary for}\\,\\underbrace{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,\\underbrace{(x-1)(x+1)=0,}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{it is necessary that}\\,\\underbrace{x=-1}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,\\underbrace{x=-1,}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{it is sufficient that}\\,\\underbrace{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S⇒N:$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option “$x=-1$ is sufficient for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$” reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x=-1}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is sufficient for}\\,\\underbrace{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option “$x=-1$ is necessary for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$” reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x=-1}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is necessary for}\\,\\underbrace{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option “For $(x-1)(x+1)=0,$ it is necessary that $x=-1$” reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,\\underbrace{(x-1)(x+1)=0,}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{it is necessary that}\\,\\underbrace{x=-1}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option “For $x=-1,$ it is sufficient that $(x-1)(x+1)=0$” reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,\\underbrace{x=-1,}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{it is sufficient that}\\,\\underbrace{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$x=-1$ is sufficient for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$” only."] [:db/cas 17592186475223 :answer-field/key "I" "$x=-1$ is sufficient for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$"] [:db/cas 17592186475224 :answer-field/key "II" "$x=-1$ is necessary for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$"] [:db/cas 17592186475225 :answer-field/key "III" "For $(x-1)(x+1)=0,$ it is necessary that $x=-1$"] [:db/cas 17592186475226 :answer-field/key "IV" "For $x=-1,$ it is sufficient that $(x-1)(x+1)=0$"] [:db/cas 17592186421142 :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=2$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}=4$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n- **I.** ${x}^{2}=4$ implies $x=2$\n- **II.** If ${x}^{2}=4,$ then $x=2$\n- **III.** ${x}^{2}=4$ only if $x=2$\n- **IV.** ${x}^{2}=4$ if $x=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=2$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}=4$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresse